NAME
       tail - print the last lines of a file

SYNOPSIS
       tail [-n lines] [file ...]

DESCRIPTION
       Writes the last 10 lines of each FILE to standard output. With
       no FILE, or with - as FILE, standard input is read.

OPTIONS
       -n N   print the last N lines (default 10)
       -N     shorthand for -n N

SEE ALSO
       head(1), less(1), watch(1)
